Visual standard: a vivid, deliberately designed travel flyer built as a premium cut-paper and Photoshop-style collage. Use layered photographic cutouts, crisp paper edges, subtle print texture, bold Caribbean blue, coral, sun yellow, and deep navy. Keep one coherent type system, color family, and graphic rhythm across the carousel, while giving each card a distinct focal story. Make the composition visibly illustrative and editorial rather than pretending to be one untouched documentary photograph. Use attached references only to preserve the real ship or named destination identity. If two destinations are shown, separate them as clear postcard panels or collage layers; never merge them into one fictional place. Do not add any text beyond the exact headline and supplied support line. Do not add fine print, logos, character likenesses, maps, QR codes, prices, badges, icons, invented landmarks, extra destinations, or claims. Preserve exact spelling and punctuation.
